      ":question/problem": "Suppose we would like to find the maximum of the function $f(x, y, z) = xy^{2}z$ on the intersection of the surfaces $x^{2} - 2z^{2} = 1$ and $y^{2} + 3z^{3} = 5$ using the method of Lagrange multipliers. Then, the corresponding Lagrange multipliers $\u03bb$ and $\u03bc$ satisfy the following system:\n\n${\u27e8y^{2}z, A A, xy^{2}\u27e9 = \u03bb\u27e82x, 0, A A\u27e9 + \u03bc\u27e80, 2y, A A\u27e9; x^{2} - 2z^{2} = 1; y^{2} + 3z^{3} = 5$\n\nFrom left to right, what are the missing parts of the expressions?"
